# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/bonds/friends.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lyra_who_beat_her
# en: Who Beat Her
title [dd3b8e] = 谁赢了她
# en: Lyra is on a window seat with an old duelling programme, soft from being folded and unfolded. The Winter Trials, the year before she came here. Second place: L. Vaneshade. "My mother wrote the week after," she says, without looking up. "Not to ask how I was. To ask who beat me."
text [22c475] = 莱拉坐在窗台上，手里一份旧决斗秩序册，折了又展、展了又折，已经软了。冬季考核，她来这里的前一年。第二名：L.凡妮希德。“一周后我母亲写信来，”她头也不抬地说，“不是问我怎么样。是问谁赢了我。”
# en: A red-haired student on a window seat holding an old folded duelling programme, soft from handling, her thumb over one line.
scene [b1650e] = 一个红发学生坐在窗台上，手里一份翻得发软的旧决斗秩序册，拇指按着其中一行。
# en: Ask who did
opt.left.label [2247f3] = 问是谁赢了她
# en: "A boy from a fishing town who never duelled again," she says. "He was better that day. I've thought about him every day since." She folds the programme along its old creases. "I hope he's happy. I hope he never thinks about it at all."
opt.left.say.1 [f2c291] = “一个渔村来的男孩，后来再没决斗过，”她说，“那天他比我强。从那以后我每天都会想起他。”她把秩序册沿着旧折痕折好。“我希望他过得开心。我希望他压根不会想起这件事。”
# en: Ask what she wrote back
opt.right.label [c58ac6] = 问她回信写了什么
# en: "His name," Lyra says. "What else?" She walks away. Later you see her at the practice ring, alone, long after the torches are out.
opt.right.say.1 [43dfee] = “他的名字，”莱拉说，“不然还能写什么？”她走开了。后来你看见她独自在练习场，火把灭了很久，她还在。

@event lyra_well_done
# en: Well Done
title [842677] = 做得好
# en: Lyra comes second in an exhibition bout, to a fourth-year twice her size, and comes off the ring with her face set like stone. Nobody says anything to her. They know better. You know her mother has never once said the two words.
text [607a59] = 莱拉在一场表演赛里输给一个比她高大一倍的四年级生，拿了第二，下场时脸绷得像石头。没人跟她说话。大家都知道最好别说。你知道，她母亲从没对她说过那三个字。
# en: A practice ring at dusk, a red-haired duellist sitting on the edge with her wand across her knees, another student holding out a cup of water.
scene [c024a3] = 黄昏的练习场，一个红发决斗者坐在场边，魔杖横在膝上，另一个学生递过去一杯水。
# en: Say them
opt.left.label [779a02] = 说出那三个字
# en: "Well done," you say. She looks at you as if you've spoken another language. Then she sits down very suddenly on the edge of the ring, and laughs, and doesn't stop for a while, and when she does her eyes are wet. "Don't," she says. "Don't you dare tell anyone."
opt.left.say.1 [e1bf8d] = “做得好。”你说。她看着你，好像你说的是外语。然后她一下子坐在场边，笑了起来，笑了好一阵，停下时眼睛湿了。“别，”她说，“你敢告诉任何人试试。”
# en: Spar with her until she's won something
opt.right.label [8b09bc] = 陪她对练到她赢为止
# en: You don't say anything. You pick up a practice wand. She beats you four times running, harder each time, and after the fourth she's breathing easier. "Thank you," she says, which is as close as she gets.
opt.right.say.1 [463665] = 你什么都没说，拿起一根练习杖。她连赢你四局，一局比一局狠，到第四局她的呼吸平顺了。“谢谢。”她说——这已经是她能说到的极限。

@event lyra_study_hall_truce
# en: The Study Hall Truce
title [4a0fc5] = 自习室停战协定
# en: Lyra has built a wall of books down the middle of your library table. "My side," she says. "Your side. No talking." {~Twenty minutes later she slides a note over the wall: "What did Thorne mean by the second law?"|An hour in, a biscuit appears on your side of the wall, unexplained.}
text [63f9f1] = 莱拉在你们的图书馆长桌中间用书垒了一道墙。“我这边，”她说，“你那边。不许说话。”{~二十分钟后，她从墙上递过来一张纸条：“索恩说的第二定律是什么意思？”|一个钟头后，你这边莫名其妙地多了一块饼干。}
# en: Two students at opposite ends of a long library table, a line of books stacked down the middle like a wall, both pretending not to look over.
scene [fb20e7] = 两个学生坐在一张图书馆长桌的两端，桌子中间一摞书垒成一道墙，两人都假装不往对面看。
# en: Answer over the wall
opt.left.label [fcc080] = 隔着墙回答她
# en: {~You write the answer and slide it back. She writes a better one and slides that back. By closing time the wall is gone and you've both written an essay neither of you could have alone.|You pass notes over the wall all evening, half about Thorne and half not. She keeps the notes. You see them later, pinned in her book.}
opt.left.say.1 [2db8ed] = {~你写好答案递回去。她写了个更好的递回来。到闭馆时墙已经没了，你们合写出一篇谁也写不出来的论文。|你们隔着墙传了一晚上纸条，一半关于索恩，一半不是。她把纸条都留着。后来你看见它们夹在她的书里。}
# en: Near midnight you slide one more note over the wall: "Bed." She reads it twice, glares at you, and, for once, goes.
opt.left.say.2 [a3c67d] = 快到午夜时，你又从书墙那边递过去一张字条：“睡觉。”她读了两遍，瞪了你一眼，然后破天荒地去睡了。
# en: Keep to your side
opt.right.label [419f2b] = 守住你那边
# en: {~You keep to your side and get more done than in a week. So does she. At closing she looks almost disappointed that you didn't break the truce.|Silence, all evening. Your notes have never been better. Lyra packs up first and doesn't say goodnight, then comes back and says it.}
opt.right.say.1 [c36156] = {~你守着你那边，一晚上干的活比一周还多。她也是。闭馆时她看上去几乎有点失望你没打破协定。|一整晚都很安静。你的笔记从没这么好过。莱拉先收拾好，没说晚安，又折回来说了。}

@event lyra_become_close
# en: Let It Run
title [a021c6] = 由它燃吧
# en: It's 3am. You find Lyra on the battlements, making a small flame walk across her knuckles. "I can't sleep," she says. "I've never told anyone that. Vaneshades sleep exactly eight hours." The flame wavers. "My grandmother had a spell she only taught to people she trusted. I've never had anyone to teach it to."
text [858d17] = 凌晨三点。你在城垛上找到莱拉，她让一小簇火在指节上走来走去。“我睡不着，”她说，“我从没告诉过任何人。凡妮希德家的人每天恰好睡八个钟头。”火苗晃了晃。“我祖母有个咒语，只教给她信任的人。我从来没有人可以教。”
# en: Two friends on a castle battlement at 3am, one of them making a small flame dance between her fingers, lighting both their faces.
scene [5c03fc] = 凌晨三点的城堡城垛上，两个朋友并肩坐着，其中一个让一小簇火在指间舞动，照亮两人的脸。
# en: Tell her she doesn't owe you anything
opt.left.label [12406b] = 告诉她她不欠你什么
# en: "I know," she says. "That's why I'd want to." But she lets the flame go out, and you sit there until the sky greys, and she doesn't mention the spell again, not yet.
opt.left.say.1 [42b1d3] = “我知道，”她说，“所以我才会想。”可她让火灭了，你们一直坐到天色发灰，她没再提那个咒语，暂时没有。
# en: Stay until sunrise
opt.right.label [b5c233] = 陪她到日出
# en: You talk until the sun comes up over the lake. About her grandmother, about fire that isn't for showing off, about being tired. When the light comes, she says, "Wildfire. That's the spell. When you're ready." She means it as the biggest thing she has.
opt.right.say.1 [4a34b7] = 你们一直聊到太阳从湖面升起。聊她的祖母，聊不是为了炫耀的火，聊累。天亮时她说：“野火。就是那个咒语。等你准备好。”她是把她最大的东西交给了你。

@event tobias_moonflower_vigil
# en: Every Eleven Years
title [a3be6f] = 每十一年一次
# en: Tobias is sitting in the greenhouse at night, beside a bed of tight pale buds, with a flask and a blanket. "Moonflowers," he says. "Once every eleven years. Could be tonight. Could be next spring." He's been coming every night for a month.
text [e1fcc8] = 夜里，托比亚斯坐在温室里一片紧闭的苍白花苞旁，带着一个水壶和一条毯子。“月光花，”他说，“十一年才开一次。可能是今晚。也可能是明年春天。”他已经每晚都来，来了一个月了。
# en: A greenhouse at night lit by one lantern, a broad-shouldered student sitting on an upturned pot beside a bed of tightly closed pale buds.
scene [68009c] = 夜里的温室只点着一盏灯，一个宽肩膀的学生坐在倒扣的花盆上，身旁是一片紧闭的苍白花苞。
# en: Keep watch with him
opt.left.label [7a29b3] = 陪他守着
# en: You keep watch until the lantern runs out. They don't bloom. Tobias isn't disappointed. "That's the point," he says. "You wait for them. They don't wait for you." He tucks the blanket round you both.
opt.left.say.1 [ce9d45] = 你陪他守到灯油燃尽。花没开。托比亚斯并不失望。“意义就在这儿，”他说，“是你等它们。它们不等你。”他把毯子裹在你们俩身上。
# en: Bring him a proper dinner
opt.right.label [c45fb4] = 给他带顿像样的晚饭
# en: You bring a pie from the kitchens. He eats it with real gratitude, and tells you about his mother's moonflowers at home, which never bloomed either, and how she kept the bed weeded for twenty years anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [1fcdfa] = 你从厨房带来一个馅饼。他吃得满怀感激，跟你讲起他母亲在老家种的月光花，也从没开过，可她照样除了二十年的草。

@event tobias_moonflower_bloom
# en: Tonight
title [56e80a] = 就是今晚
# en: Tobias bangs on your door after dark. "Tonight," he says. "They're opening. Come on. Come ON." He's already running. In the greenhouse the moonflowers are unfolding, one by one, silver at the edges, and the whole place smells like rain.
text [9f39f0] = 天黑后托比亚斯砰砰敲你的门。“今晚，”他说，“它们要开了。快来。快来啊。”他已经跑出去了。温室里，月光花一朵接一朵地舒展开来，边缘泛着银光，整个屋子闻起来像雨。
# en: A greenhouse at midnight full of pale open blossoms glowing faintly silver, a big student standing among them with his mouth open.
scene [53d064] = 午夜的温室里开满了苍白的花，微微泛着银光，一个高大的学生站在花丛中张着嘴。
# en: Run with him
opt.left.label [8039e4] = 跟他一起跑
# en: You run. You're in time. Every bud opens while you watch, and the greenhouse glows, and Tobias doesn't say a word for an hour. At the end he says, "Eleven years," and then, "Thank you for waiting with me," as if you'd done the waiting. You'll remember it longer than anything you were meant to study tonight.
opt.left.say.1 [0c8ab7] = 你跑了起来。赶上了。每一个花苞都在你们眼前打开，温室亮了，托比亚斯一个钟头没说一句话。最后他说：“十一年。”然后：“谢谢你陪我等。”好像等的是你。你会记得这一晚，比今晚本该温习的任何东西都久。
# en: Tell him to go; you'll catch up
opt.right.label [370f56] = 叫他先去，你随后到
# en: You finish your essay first. By the time you get there, half are open and Tobias is crying, quietly, the happy way. He saves you the best one to watch. It opens just for you, he insists. You don't argue.
opt.right.say.1 [fe8f50] = 你先写完了论文。等你赶到时，花已经开了一半，托比亚斯在哭，静静地，是高兴的那种。他给你留了开得最好的那一朵。他坚持说，那一朵是只为你开的。你没争。

@event tobias_plants_vote
# en: The Greenhouse Votes
title [3db2c0] = 温室投票
# en: You've got a decision to make, and Tobias offers to ask the greenhouse. "They're good judges," he says. "Plants don't lie. They just turn towards what's good for them." He holds a seedling up to your face. {~It leans toward you, slowly.|It leans away, very slightly, and Tobias frowns.}
text [7b9ae8] = 你有个决定要做，托比亚斯提议去问问温室。“它们判断得很准，”他说，“植物不撒谎。它们只会转向对自己好的东西。”他把一株幼苗举到你面前。{~它慢慢地朝你倾过来。|它非常轻微地往后偏了偏，托比亚斯皱起眉头。}
# en: A big student in a greenhouse holding his ear close to a row of seedlings, another student watching with folded arms.
scene [44c46a] = 温室里，一个高大的学生把耳朵凑近一排幼苗，另一个学生抱着胳膊看着。
# en: Do what the seedling says
opt.left.label [bfc5ce] = 照幼苗说的做
# en: {~"Yes, then," Tobias says, satisfied. It turns out to be the right call, though you'll never be sure it was the seedling's.|"Not that, then," he says, and you don't, and you never find out what would have happened, which is how good advice usually works.}
opt.left.say.1 [ba6b5e] = {~“那就是好。”托比亚斯满意地说。结果证明这个决定是对的，虽然你永远不确定该不该归功于幼苗。|“那就不要。”他说。你没做，也永远不会知道做了会怎样——好建议通常就是这样。}
# en: Ask him what he thinks
opt.right.label [8b1202] = 问他怎么看
# en: {~"Me?" He's surprised. He thinks it through, slowly, the way he does everything. His answer is better than the seedling's. He doesn't tell the seedling.|He gives you an answer so sensible you're embarrassed you asked a plant. "Don't tell them I said that," he whispers.}
opt.right.say.1 [2e1bd9] = {~“我？”他很意外。他慢慢地想，像他做所有事一样。他的答案比幼苗的好。他没告诉幼苗。|他给出的答案合理得让你不好意思去问一株植物。“别告诉它们是我说的。”他小声说。}

@event tobias_scholarship_review
# en: The Turnip Board
title [9ff69e] = 萝卜奖学金委员会
# en: Tobias has a letter from the agricultural scholarship board: a review of his marks, next week, in person. "If they take it away I go home," he says. "Not that home's bad. But I'm not done here." He's opened four textbooks and read none of them.
text [aa3f2f] = 托比亚斯收到农业奖学金委员会的信：下周当面复审他的成绩。“要是他们收回奖学金，我就得回家，”他说，“倒不是家里不好。可我在这儿还没完。”他翻开了四本课本，一本都没读进去。
# en: A big student at a library table with a letter on top of a pile of open textbooks, head in his hands.
scene [33a7be] = 一个高大的学生坐在图书馆桌前，一封信压在一堆摊开的课本上，双手抱着头。
# en: Drill him all week
opt.left.label [6b5389] = 陪他操练一整周
# en: You drill him every night. At the review he answers everything, slowly and right, and one of the board members, a farmer herself, shakes his hand. He brings you a turnip. It's the best turnip you've ever had.
opt.left.say.1 [2e1e75] = 你每晚陪他操练。复审时他每个问题都答上了，慢，但是对，一位委员——她自己也是农夫——和他握了手。他送你一个萝卜。是你吃过最好的萝卜。
# en: You drill him, but the board is hard. He keeps the scholarship on probation. "Probation's fine," he says. "Probation means I'm still here." He hugs you anyway, which lifts you off the floor.
opt.left.say.2 [5b8a79] = 你陪他操练了，可委员会很严。他的奖学金保住了，但处于察看期。“察看挺好，”他说，“察看就是说我还在这儿。”他照样给了你一个拥抱，把你抱离了地面。
# en: Write to the board for him
opt.right.label [2e91a7] = 替他给委员会写信
# en: You write a letter about the boy who keeps the greenhouse alive and talks the mandrakes through exams. He never knows you sent it. The board renews him with a note about "character", and he can't think why.
opt.right.say.1 [130617] = 你写了封信，讲那个让温室活下来、在考试时给曼德拉草打气的男孩。他永远不知道是你寄的。委员会续了他的奖学金，附注里提到“品格”，他想不通为什么。
# en: You put in the moonflowers, and the storm, and how he held the greenhouse door shut with his whole body. The board, it turns out, has farmers on it.
opt.right.say.2 [74d879] = 你在信里写了月光花，写了那场风暴，写了他怎样用整个身子顶住温室的门。原来委员会里也有农民。

@event seraphine_oracle_letter
# en: A Letter From Vell
title [2ba9f9] = 维尔来信
# en: Seraphine has a letter with a silver seal. She hasn't opened it. "My mother," she says. "She's the Oracle of Vell. She tells kings what they want to hear and they pay her in castles. She wants me home, to learn it." She turns it over. "I already know what it says. I see it, a little, through the paper."
text [348e68] = 瑟拉芬有一封盖着银色火漆的信。她还没拆。“我母亲，”她说，“她是维尔神谕。她告诉国王们他们想听的话，他们用城堡付钱。她想让我回家学这个。”她把信翻过来。“我已经知道里面写了什么。我能隔着信纸看见一点。”
# en: A girl in a paint-stained smock holding a letter sealed in silver wax at arm's length, as if it were warm.
scene [d4d6ed] = 一个穿着沾满颜料罩衫的女孩伸直胳膊拿着一封盖银色火漆的信，好像它是热的。
# en: Ask what she wants
opt.left.label [8b24a1] = 问她想要什么
# en: Nobody has asked her that. She thinks for a long time. "To be wrong sometimes," she says. "Here, I'm wrong about small things. It's lovely." She puts the letter in a drawer, unopened. "She'll write again. She always knows when I've stopped reading."
opt.left.say.1 [472801] = 从没人问过她这个。她想了很久。“偶尔犯错，”她说，“在这里，我会在小事上出错。很美妙。”她把信放进抽屉，没拆。“她还会写的。我一不读，她总是知道。”
# en: Offer to read it to her
opt.right.label [fd46ab] = 提出替她念
# en: You read it out. It's exactly what she said it would be, word for word. "See," she says, quietly. "Nothing in it I didn't know. That's the worst part. Thank you for saying it in someone else's voice."
opt.right.say.1 [5fa884] = 你念了出来。和她说的一模一样，一字不差。“你看，”她轻声说，“没有一句是我不知道的。这才是最糟的。谢谢你用别人的声音把它说出来。”

@event seraphine_what_you_want_to_hear
# en: What You Want to Hear
title [6ffa11] = 你想听的话
# en: "My mother's trick," Seraphine says, taking your hands, eyes half-closed. "Watch. I'll tell you what you want to hear." {~"You will pass every exam, be loved by everyone and find a small dog."|"Your enemies will grow warts and your friends will grow taller."} She opens one eye. "Now. Do you want the true one?"
text [04e76a] = “我母亲的把戏，”瑟拉芬握住你的双手，半闭着眼说，“看好了。我会告诉你你想听的话。”{~“你会通过每一场考试，被所有人爱戴，还会捡到一只小狗。”|“你的敌人会长疣，你的朋友会长高。”}她睁开一只眼。“好了。你想听真的那个吗？”
# en: A seer holding both of another student's hands across a table, eyes half-closed, a theatrical candle burning between them.
scene [9bee52] = 一个预言者隔着桌子握住另一个学生的双手，半闭着眼，两人之间点着一支装模作样的蜡烛。
# en: Keep the pretty one
opt.left.label [1a0239] = 留着好听的那个
# en: {~"Wise," she says. "Kings always pick that one too." She blows out the candle with a flourish. You do, briefly, believe in the small dog.|"Good choice." She looks relieved. "The true one has a lot of rain in it."}
opt.left.say.1 [7c9cfc] = {~“明智，”她说，“国王们也总是选这个。”她潇洒地吹灭蜡烛。有那么一会儿，你真的相信会有一只小狗。|“好选择。”她看上去松了口气。“真的那个里有好多雨。”}
# en: Ask for the true one
opt.right.label [072bb6] = 要听真的那个
# en: {~"You'll be tired a lot, and it will be worth it." She lets go of your hands. "That's the only true one I'll give anyone. Nobody else asks for it."|"Something will be hard, and you'll do it anyway, and someone will be proud of you." She shrugs. "It's not much. It's true."}
opt.right.say.1 [be278d] = {~“你会经常很累，而这是值得的。”她松开你的手。“这是我唯一会给人的真话。别人都不要。”|“有件事会很难，你还是会去做，而有人会为你骄傲。”她耸耸肩。“不多。但是真的。”}

@event seraphine_too_loud
# en: Too Loud
title [a08867] = 太吵了
# en: In the middle of a full refectory Seraphine puts both hands over her ears and goes white. Nobody notices but you. "Everyone's futures," she whispers, when you get to her. "All at once. It's like a hundred people shouting what they'll be."
text [6c8b7b] = 在坐满人的膳堂中间，瑟拉芬双手捂住耳朵，脸色发白。除了你没人注意到。“大家的未来，”你走到她身边时，她低声说，“一下子全来了。像一百个人同时喊着自己将来会成为什么。”
# en: A crowded refectory at lunchtime, a girl with her hands pressed over her ears in the middle of it, everyone else oblivious.
scene [2d6ce2] = 午饭时坐满人的膳堂，一个女孩在人群中用双手捂着耳朵，其他人浑然不觉。
# en: Get her out of there
opt.left.label [729ad3] = 带她出去
# en: You walk her out into the cloister, where it's quiet. She breathes. "Yours is quiet," she says, after a while. "I've always meant to say. It's like a room with the door shut." You miss your lecture. You don't mind.
opt.left.say.1 [02599d] = 你扶着她走到回廊里，那里很安静。她喘过气来。“你的很安静，”过了一会儿她说，“我一直想告诉你。像一间关着门的屋子。”你错过了那节课。你不介意。
# en: Talk to her, loudly, about nothing
opt.right.label [63e5f8] = 大声跟她聊些闲话
# en: You talk about the soup, the weather, a dog you once knew, loudly, right next to her. It works: she can hear the now over the noise. "Keep going," she says, eyes shut. You talk about soup for twenty minutes.
opt.right.say.1 [79a07c] = 你就在她旁边，大声聊汤、聊天气、聊你以前认识的一只狗。管用：她能在噪声之上听见此刻了。“继续说。”她闭着眼说。你聊了二十分钟的汤。

@event corvin_lock_lesson
# en: Every Door
title [5fee74] = 每一扇门
# en: Corvin is crouched at the Alchemy store's door after dark, two picks in the lock. "Hold that lantern up," he says, as if you'd agreed. "There isn't a locked door in this castle I can't open. I'm not taking anything. I'm keeping in practice."
text [9cac30] = 天黑后，科尔文蹲在炼金储藏室门前，两根细撬针插在锁里。“把灯举高点。”他说，好像你已经答应了。“这城堡里没有我开不了的锁。我不拿东西。我在保持手感。”
# en: A lanky student crouched at a classroom door after dark, two thin picks in the lock, another student holding the lantern.
scene [4b366c] = 天黑后，一个瘦高的学生蹲在教室门前，锁里插着两根细撬针，另一个学生举着灯。
# en: Ask him to teach you
opt.left.label [69348f] = 请他教你
# en: He shows you how to feel the pins, one at a time. On your eleventh try the lock clicks. Corvin applauds silently. Then he locks it again, carefully, and leaves it exactly as it was. "Rule one," he says. "Always leave it how you found it."
opt.left.say.1 [eb891c] = 他教你怎么一根一根地感觉锁芯里的弹子。第十一次，锁咔嗒一声开了。科尔文无声地鼓掌。然后他又把锁仔细锁上，恢复原样。“第一条规矩，”他说，“永远让它保持你来时的样子。”
# en: Keep watch instead
opt.right.label [ad394d] = 替他望风
# en: You keep watch. He's in and out in a minute, with nothing in his hands but a single sugared almond from the jar on the master's desk. "Tradition," he says. He splits it with you.
opt.right.say.1 [e1435d] = 你替他望风。他一分钟就进出了，手里什么都没拿，只有讲师桌上罐子里的一颗糖杏仁。“传统。”他说。他分了你一半。

@event corvin_takes_the_blame
# en: One More Detention
title [267a14] = 再关一次禁闭
# en: Professor Vey holds up a set of lock picks found outside the Restricted Section. "Whose?" Corvin opens his mouth to make a joke, and you remember: one more detention and he's sent home, and home is not a good place.
text [71350e] = 维伊教授举起一套在禁书区外捡到的撬锁工具。“谁的？”科尔文张嘴要开玩笑，而你想起来了：再关一次禁闭，他就会被送回家，而家不是个好地方。
# en: A stern professor in a corridor holding up a confiscated set of lock picks, two students in front of her, one of them grinning too widely.
scene [033f46] = 走廊里，一位严厉的教授举着一套没收的撬锁工具，面前站着两个学生，其中一个笑得太过灿烂。
# en: "They're mine."
opt.left.label [6d9cc8] = “是我的。”
# en: Vey looks at you for a long moment, and at Corvin, and writes your name down. Corvin doesn't speak to you all day. That night there's a note under your door. It says "I owe you" and, underneath, smaller, "I'm not joking."
opt.left.say.1 [ae3edd] = 维伊看了你很久，又看了看科尔文，写下了你的名字。科尔文一整天没跟你说话。那晚你门下塞进一张纸条，写着“我欠你的”，下面一行小字：“我没开玩笑。”
# en: Let him talk his way out
opt.right.label [0c2a2d] = 让他自己圆过去
# en: He talks. It's a masterpiece: picks, a jackdaw, a misunderstanding about a cupboard. Vey doesn't believe a word and lets him go anyway, for the performance.
opt.right.say.1 [d5901e] = 他开口了。堪称杰作：撬针、一只寒鸦、一场关于橱柜的误会。维伊一个字都不信，但为了这场表演放他走了。
# en: He talks, and it doesn't work. Vey can't prove the picks are his, so there's no detention; she keeps them, and writes his name in a little book. He laughs it off. His hands shake for the rest of the day.
opt.right.say.2 [d0b1b6] = 他开口了，可没用。维伊证明不了开锁器是他的，所以没有禁闭；她把开锁器收了，在一个小本子上记下他的名字。他一笑置之。那一整天他的手都在抖。

@event corvin_cartographer_hint
# en: The Club That Doesn't Exist
title [475340] = 不存在的社团
# en: There's a map in your library book that wasn't there before. Corridors you've never seen, inked in a careful hand, and in the corner, very small: "M.C. — we don't exist. Bring a lantern." Corvin, across the table, is reading upside down.
text [e45157] = 你的图书馆借书里多了一张原本没有的地图。一些你从没见过的走廊，用工整的笔迹画出，角落里很小的一行字：“午夜制图社——我们不存在。带盏灯。”桌对面的科尔文正倒着看书。
# en: A folded map slipped into a book in a library, the margins full of tiny inked doors, a lanky student pretending not to have left it.
scene [4027d7] = 图书馆的一本书里夹着一张折好的地图，页边画满小小的门，一个瘦高的学生假装不是他放的。
# en: Ask him outright
opt.left.label [fa721a] = 直接问他
# en: "Never heard of them," he says. "Terrible people. Midnight, the third gargoyle on the left. Don't bring anyone." He goes back to his upside-down book. He's grinning at it.
opt.left.say.1 [3bacd8] = “从没听说过，”他说，“一群可怕的人。午夜，左边第三座石像鬼。别带别人。”他继续看他倒着的书。他在对着书咧嘴笑。
# en: Follow the map alone
opt.right.label [4cacb2] = 独自照着地图走
# en: You follow it into a passage that smells of old candle wax, and bark your shin on a step that isn't on the map. At the end, someone has chalked "TOLD YOU" on the wall. It's in Corvin's handwriting.
opt.right.say.1 [fd3c10] = 你照着它走进一条散发着旧蜡烛味的通道，在一级地图上没画的台阶上磕了小腿。尽头的墙上有人用粉笔写着“早告诉你了”。是科尔文的笔迹。

@event mir_small_fire
# en: A Small Fire
title [0853d5] = 一场小火
# en: There's a small fire on Mir's workbench. Mir is looking at it with interest. "It's fine," they say. "It's a controlled fire. I'm controlling it by watching it." The fire grows. "I'm watching it harder."
text [5eb966] = 米尔的工作台上着了一小团火。米尔饶有兴致地看着它。“没事，”TA说，“这是可控的火。我在通过看着它来控制它。”火变大了。“我看得更用力了。”
# en: A workbench with a tiny cheerful fire burning in the middle of it, an artificer in goggles looking at it with professional interest rather than alarm.
scene [808187] = 工作台中央欢快地燃着一小团火，戴护目镜的奇械师用专业的兴趣而非惊慌看着它。
# en: Put it out
opt.left.label [baa0ef] = 把火扑灭
# en: You smother it with a lab coat. Mir sighs, and writes "fire: yes" in a notebook, under a long column of "fire: no". "That's useful data," they say, sincerely. "Thank you for ruining it."
opt.left.say.1 [f50ed3] = 你用实验服把火捂灭了。米尔叹了口气，在笔记本上长长一列“着火：否”的下面写下“着火：是”。“这是有用的数据，”TA真诚地说，“谢谢你毁了它。”
# en: Ask what it was meant to be
opt.right.label [360171] = 问它本来是要做什么
# en: "A kettle," they say, as the fire eats the kettle. "A self-heating kettle." The bucket under the bench, it turns out, is always full for exactly this reason.
opt.right.say.1 [644191] = “一把水壶，”TA说，火正在吞掉那把水壶，“一把自加热水壶。”原来，工作台底下那桶水永远是满的，就是为了这个。

@event mir_padlock
# en: The Padlock
title [175fe6] = 挂锁
# en: Mir's workshop is still padlocked, and whatever they've been making do with isn't working: they've been soldering in the corridor outside the old door, on the floor, for a week. "It's fine," they say, soldering on their knee. "It's character-building. My character is very built."
text [50e6a3] = 米尔的工坊还挂着锁，而TA凑合用的地方也不管用：TA已经在旧门外的走廊地上焊了一周的东西。“没事，”TA一边在膝盖上焊接一边说，“磨炼品格。我的品格已经磨炼得很好了。”
# en: An artificer sitting on the floor outside a padlocked door, back against it, notebooks stacked beside them, a student coming down the corridor with a box.
scene [6e94fe] = 一个奇械师背靠着一扇挂了锁的门坐在地上，身边摞着笔记本，另一个学生抱着一个箱子从走廊那头走来。
# en: Give them your desk
opt.left.label [3517b2] = 把你的书桌让给TA
# en: You clear the desk in your room and carry their boxes up four flights. Mir moves in within the hour. The first thing they build there is a sign: "Workshop. Fires: probably fine." You do your reading on the stairs for a month.
opt.left.say.1 [0a1e87] = 你清空了房间里的书桌，把TA的箱子搬上四层楼。一个钟头内米尔就搬了进来。TA在那里造的第一件东西是一块牌子：“工坊。着火：大概没事。”接下来一个月你都在楼梯上看书。
# en: Ward the workshop and prove it
opt.right.label [964c83] = 给工坊加护咒并证明给他看
# en: Make the old room safe, and show Thorne.
opt.right.hint [794539] = 让旧房间变安全，再给索恩看。
# en: You spend a week warding every bench. Thorne lights a match on the worst one, watches it go out on its own, sighs like a dying bellows and hands Mir the key. "Bucket within reach," he says. They keep three.
opt.right.say.1 [c95f0b] = 你花了一周给每张工作台加上护咒。索恩在最糟的那张上划了根火柴，看着它自己熄灭，叹了口气，像一只快没气的风箱，把钥匙交给了米尔。“手边放一桶水，”他说。TA放了三桶。
# en: The ward holds until it doesn't. Thorne puts out the bench with one hand and files the request with the other. But you sit in the corridor with Mir that evening and hand them screws, and it's less fine with company.
opt.right.say.2 [88acb8] = 护咒撑住了，直到撑不住。索恩一只手扑灭了工作台，另一只手把申请归了档。可那晚你在走廊里陪米尔坐着，给TA递螺丝，有人陪着就没那么有事了。

@event mir_family_clocks
# en: Not a Hobby
title [249789] = 不是爱好
# en: {flag(mir_family_wrote): Mir's mother has named her prize: the guild medal for young artificers, entries closing in a fortnight. Mir has three inventions half-built and no time. "Win a prize," they mutter, to a clock. "Win a prize."|A letter from Mir's father, the first he's ever written them himself: could they send something they've made, to show the men at the clockworks? Mir has started the reply four times.}
text [855db5] = {flag(mir_family_wrote): 米尔的母亲说出了她要的奖：给年轻奇械师的行会奖章，两周后截止报名。米尔有三件做了一半的发明，却没有时间。“拿个奖，”TA对着一只钟嘟囔，“拿个奖。”|米尔的父亲来了封信，这是他第一次亲手给TA写信：能不能寄一件TA做的东西来，好给作坊里的人看看？米尔的回信已经开了四次头。}
# en: A letter on a workbench, held down by a small brass clock, the artificer reading it with their goggles pushed up and their jaw tight.
scene [c3aa64] = 工作台上一封信被一只小黄铜钟压着，奇械师把护目镜推到额头上读着信，下巴绷得紧紧的。
# en: Help them write it up
opt.left.label [9c261d] = 帮TA写出来
# en: {flag(mir_family_wrote): You write up the entry together, all evening: what it does, why it matters, who'll use it. It's three pages and not one apology. "Whatever the judges say," Mir says, "it's finished."|You write it together, all evening: what Mir built this year, what it does, who uses it. Three pages of inventions and not one apology. "He'll read every word," Mir says. "Twice. He reads instructions twice."}
opt.left.say.1 [37f998] = {flag(mir_family_wrote): 你们一起写参赛说明，写了一整晚：它能做什么，为什么重要，谁会用它。三页纸，没有一句道歉。“不管评委怎么说，”米尔说，“它完成了。”|你们一起写了一整晚：米尔今年造了什么，能做什么，谁在用。三页纸全是发明，没有一句道歉。“他会一字一字地读，”米尔说，“读两遍。说明书他都读两遍。”}
# en: Tell them to send the owl
opt.right.label [573578] = 叫TA把猫头鹰寄去
# en: {flag(mir_family_wrote): They send in the brass owl. It comes second. Mir's mother writes back one line: "Second is a prize." Mir frames it.|Mir looks at the brass owl on the shelf for a long time. Then they wrap it and post it. The letter back is very short: "Dad cried. He says it's not a hobby. I said I know."} You miss the owl on the shelf.
opt.right.say.1 [1cfc54] = {flag(mir_family_wrote): TA把黄铜猫头鹰送去参赛。得了第二名。米尔的母亲回信只有一行：“第二名也是奖。”米尔把它裱了起来。|米尔盯着架子上的黄铜猫头鹰看了很久。然后TA把它包好寄了出去。回信很短：“爸爸哭了。他说这不是爱好。我说我知道。”}架子上少了那只猫头鹰，你有点想它。

@event kael_northern_supper
# en: A Northern Supper
title [606d45] = 北境晚餐
# en: You find Kael in the castle kitchens after hours, cooking something dark and sour-smelling over the smallest fire. "Northern," he says. "Fish, berries, and something you don't want to know. Nobody here makes it." There's already a second bowl out.
text [ca1037] = 熄灯后你在城堡厨房里找到凯尔，他在最小的一簇火上煮着什么，颜色很深，闻着发酸。“北境的，”他说，“鱼、浆果，还有一样你不会想知道的东西。这里没人做。”第二只碗已经摆好了。
# en: A pale boy in a fur coat at the kitchen hearth late at night, carefully stirring a pot of dark broth, a second bowl set out without being asked for.
scene [56c5f1] = 深夜里，一个穿毛皮大衣的苍白男孩在厨房炉边小心地搅着一锅深色的汤，旁边没等人要就多摆了一只碗。
# en: Eat it all
opt.left.label [187f65] = 全都吃光
# en: It's the strangest thing you've ever eaten. You finish the bowl. Kael watches you with an expression you've never seen on him: hope. "Next time," he says, "I'll tell you what was in it." You hope he doesn't.
opt.left.say.1 [cbe032] = 这是你吃过最古怪的东西。你吃完了一整碗。凯尔看着你，脸上是你从没见过的神情：希望。“下次，”他说，“我告诉你里面有什么。”你希望他别说。
# en: Ask him to tell you about home
opt.right.label [237455] = 请他讲讲家乡
# en: He tells you about winter that lasts eight months and summer that lasts eight days, and singing on the ice to keep the dark back. He doesn't mention his family once. You notice. You don't ask.
opt.right.say.1 [2201dd] = 他跟你讲八个月的冬天和八天的夏天，讲人们在冰上唱歌把黑暗挡在外面。他一次都没提到他的家人。你注意到了。你没问。

@event kael_gloves
# en: Gloves
title [0edcb7] = 手套
# en: Kael's hands are so cold the ink in his pen keeps freezing in lectures. You've noticed. He's noticed you noticing. Winter's coming, and he still doesn't own a pair of gloves.
text [ed9a39] = 凯尔的手冷得让他上课时笔里的墨水一直结冰。你注意到了。他也注意到你注意到了。冬天要来了，他还是没有一副手套。
# en: A pair of thick knitted gloves, slightly lopsided, on a pale boy's hands as he turns them over and over, frost beginning to form on the wool.
scene [8905a8] = 一副厚厚的手织手套，有点歪，戴在一个苍白男孩的手上，他翻来覆去地看，毛线上开始结霜。
# en: Knit him some
opt.left.label [795b79] = 给他织一副
# en: They take a month and are lopsided. Frost forms on the wool within the hour. He wears them anyway, every day, until the thumbs wear through, and then he darns the thumbs himself, badly, rather than give them up.
opt.left.say.1 [2e5d91] = 织了一个月，还织歪了。一个钟头内毛线上就结了霜。他还是每天戴着，直到拇指磨破，然后他自己笨手笨脚地补好拇指，也不肯换。
# en: Buy him some in the village
opt.right.label [57d15d] = 去镇上给他买一副
# en: You buy a good warm pair. He holds them as if no one had ever given him a thing just for being cold. "I don't feel it, mostly," he says. He wears them anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [d42760] = 你买了一副暖和的好手套。他捧着它们，好像从没有人只因为他冷就送他东西。“我大多时候感觉不到。”他说。他还是戴上了。

@event kael_frost_fern
# en: The Frost-Fern Trick
title [aeec3f] = 霜蕨把戏
# en: Kael shows you a children's trick from the North: you draw on a frosted window and the frost finishes the drawing for you. {~He draws a line; the frost turns it into a fern.|You draw a circle; the frost turns it into a snowflake the size of your hand.}
text [843f79] = 凯尔教你一个北境的儿童把戏：在结霜的窗上画画，霜会替你画完。{~他画一道线；霜把它变成一片蕨叶。|你画一个圈；霜把它变成一片巴掌大的雪花。}
# en: A frosted window in a common room, a pale boy and another student drawing on it with their fingertips, ferns of ice spreading from each line.
scene [56790a] = 公共休息室一扇结霜的窗前，一个苍白的男孩和另一个学生用指尖在上面画画，每一笔都长出冰蕨。
# en: Draw something silly
opt.left.label [0600e8] = 画个傻东西
# en: {~You draw a goat. The frost, after a moment's thought, gives it a magnificent beard. Kael makes a sound you've never heard from him. It's a laugh.|You draw Professor Thorne. The frost gives him icicles for eyebrows. Kael has to sit down.}
opt.left.say.1 [8a855a] = {~你画了只山羊。霜想了想，给它添了一把威风的胡子。凯尔发出一个你从没听过的声音。是笑声。|你画了索恩教授。霜给他添了冰柱眉毛。凯尔不得不坐下。}
# en: Ask him how it works
opt.right.label [acef1d] = 问他原理
# en: {~"You don't make it," he says. "You let it. Frost wants to grow. You show it where." He's a better teacher than he thinks.|He explains, slowly, and then guides your hand. The frost follows your finger like a cat. "There," he says. "You're Northern now. A bit."}
opt.right.say.1 [b68818] = {~“不是你造出来的，”他说，“是你让它长。霜想长。你指给它方向。”他比他自己以为的会教。|他慢慢讲解，然后握着你的手引导。霜像猫一样跟着你的手指走。“好了，”他说，“你现在是北境人了。一点点。”}

@event nessa_interview_prep
# en: Twenty Years
title [5fb846] = 二十年
# en: Nessa has two hundred questions for the headmistress, pinned to her wall. "Nobody's interviewed her in twenty years," she says. "I'll get one chance. I have to pick the question that matters." She's crossed out a hundred and ninety.
text [0e5447] = 内莎有两百个问题要问院长，全钉在她墙上。“二十年没人采访过她，”她说，“我只有一次机会。我得挑出真正要紧的那个问题。”她已经划掉了一百九十个。
# en: A girl in an untidy office with a long list of questions pinned to a wall, crossing out most of them, another student reading over her shoulder.
scene [4317ff] = 一间凌乱的办公室里，一个女孩把一长串问题钉在墙上，把大部分划掉，另一个学生从她肩后看着。
# en: Help her pick
opt.left.label [fd3e52] = 帮她挑
# en: You go through the last ten together until midnight. The one you pick is very simple: "What do you wish students asked you?" Nessa stares at it. "That's either the best question I've ever asked or the worst," she says. "Good."
opt.left.say.1 [15360d] = 你们一起把最后十个过了一遍，一直到午夜。你们挑中的那个非常简单：“您希望学生问您什么？”内莎盯着它。“这要么是我问过最好的问题，要么是最糟的，”她说，“很好。”
# en: Play the headmistress for practice
opt.right.label [beaff8] = 扮演院长陪她练
# en: You play the headmistress, badly, with a pencil for a wand. Nessa grills you for an hour and makes you cry with laughter twice and nearly cry the other way once. "She'll be harder," she says. "She'll be you, but calmer."
opt.right.say.1 [963911] = 你扮演院长，演得很糟，拿一支铅笔当魔杖。内莎盘问了你一个钟头，有两次让你笑出了眼泪，有一次差点让你哭出来。“她会更难对付，”她说，“她会是你，只是更冷静。”

@event nessa_fact_check
# en: Fact-Check
title [06d856] = 事实核查
# en: Nessa slaps a proof down in front of you. "Fact-check it. I don't trust my quill and I don't trust me." {~It's an article about the history of the castle's founding.|It's a profile of the Duelling Circle's captain.} There are, she warns you, at least three errors, and one of them is planted, to see if you're paying attention.
text [8f25b1] = 内莎把一份校样拍在你面前。“核查一下。我不信我的羽毛笔，也不信我自己。”{~是一篇关于城堡建校史的文章。|是一篇决斗社社长的人物特写。}她警告你，里面至少有三处错误，其中一处是故意埋的，看你有没有用心。
# en: A newspaper proof covered in red-ink circles, a girl handing it across a desk to another student with a pencil behind her ear.
scene [130535] = 一份画满红墨圈的报纸校样，一个耳后夹着铅笔的女孩隔着书桌把它递给另一个学生。
# en: Go through it properly
opt.left.label [f2d0e0] = 好好核一遍
# en: {~You find all three, and a fourth she didn't plant. Nessa looks at you with something close to love, the editorial kind. "Staff," she says. "You're staff now."|You find the planted one first, then the others. Nessa writes "GOOD" on your hand in red ink. It takes three days to wash off.}
opt.left.say.1 [ad7f38] = {~三处你全找到了，还找出一处她没埋的。内莎看着你，眼神近乎爱慕，编辑式的那种。“编辑部的人，”她说，“你现在是编辑部的人了。”|你先找到了埋的那处，然后是另外两处。内莎用红墨水在你手背上写了个“好”。洗了三天才洗掉。}
# en: {~You find two. The planted one gets past you. Nessa circles it, gleefully, and tells you why it was obvious. You learn more from that than from the article.|You find one, and mark a true fact as wrong. Nessa is delighted: now she has to check it again, and it's still true, and she likes being right twice.}
opt.left.say.2 [895615] = {~你找到两处。埋的那处从你眼皮底下溜了过去。内莎兴高采烈地把它圈出来，告诉你它为什么一目了然。你从中学到的比从文章里学到的还多。|你找到一处，还把一个正确的事实标成了错的。内莎高兴极了：现在她得再核查一遍，结果它还是对的，而她喜欢对两次。}
# en: Hand it back: "It's fine."
opt.right.label [ab97b9] = 还给她：“没问题。”
# en: {~"Nothing's fine," Nessa says. She takes it back and finds all three in five minutes. "Lazy," she says, but she's smiling.|She looks at you over the proof. "That's what my quill says," she says. "I don't trust it either."}
opt.right.say.1 [6e3028] = {~“什么都有问题。”内莎说。她拿回去，五分钟就找出了三处。“偷懒。”她说，但她在笑。|她从校样上方看着你。“我的羽毛笔也这么说，”她说，“我也不信它。”}

@event nessa_quill_loose
# en: The Quill Gets Loose
title [52889c] = 羽毛笔跑了
# en: Nessa's quill has escaped. It's loose in the castle, writing news. You've seen three of its headlines on the walls already: "PROFESSOR'S CAT IS SECRETLY A PROFESSOR", "LAKE: TOO WET?", and one about you that isn't true but is, you have to admit, flattering.
text [0367af] = 内莎的羽毛笔逃跑了。它在城堡里乱窜，到处写新闻。你已经在墙上看到它的三条标题：“教授的猫其实是一位教授”“湖：是否太湿？”，还有一条写你的，不是真的，但你得承认，挺讨人喜欢。
# en: An enchanted quill flying down a castle corridor trailing a long scroll, a girl chasing it with an inkpot, students ducking.
scene [af4c21] = 一支施了魔法的羽毛笔拖着一长卷纸飞过城堡走廊，一个女孩拿着墨水瓶在后面追，学生们纷纷低头躲避。
# en: Help her catch it
opt.left.label [8fa173] = 帮她抓住它
# en: You corner it in the owlery. It writes "CAUGHT" on your sleeve as you grab it. Nessa stuffs it in her inkpot and screws the lid on. "Thank you," she says, breathless. "It was going to do a horoscope page. Again."
opt.left.say.1 [c14881] = 你在猫头鹰棚把它逼进了角落。你抓住它时，它在你袖子上写了“已捕获”。内莎把它塞进墨水瓶，拧紧了盖子。“谢谢，”她气喘吁吁地说，“它又要搞星座专版了。”
# en: Leave the headline about you up
opt.right.label [ded518] = 留着写你的那条
# en: You leave it up. People read it for a week. Nessa takes it down eventually, with a look. "It made it up," she says. "You know that." You do. It's still a lovely headline.
opt.right.say.1 [6a8da3] = 你没撕。人们读了一周。最后内莎把它取了下来，看了你一眼。“它编的，”她说，“你知道的。”你知道。那还是一条很美的标题。

@event bram_portrait
# en: Head Boy, Forty Years Ago
title [5e66a0] = 四十年前的男生代表
# en: You find Bram in the corridor of head boys' portraits, in front of one in particular: a big man with Bram's jaw and none of his doubt. "He walks past this every visit," Bram says. "Stops. Looks at it. Then looks at me." He doesn't need to say the rest.
text [76dd48] = 你在历届男生代表的肖像走廊里找到布拉姆，他站在其中一幅前：一个高大的男人，有布拉姆的下颌，却没有他的半分犹疑。“他每次来都从这儿走过，”布拉姆说，“停下来。看着它。然后看着我。”剩下的话他不必说。
# en: A row of old portraits of head boys in a dim corridor, a big student in a prefect's sash standing in front of one, not moving.
scene [495874] = 昏暗的走廊里挂着一排历届男生代表的旧肖像，一个佩着级长绶带的高大学生站在其中一幅前，一动不动。
# en: Say the portrait's a bad likeness
opt.left.label [3844f0] = 说这画画得不像
# en: "It is," Bram says, surprised into it. "Painter made him look kind." He laughs, short and rough, and it changes his face. "Don't tell anyone I laughed at a portrait."
opt.left.say.1 [8e58e5] = “是不像，”布拉姆被逗得脱口而出，“画家把他画得太和善了。”他短促、粗哑地笑了一声，整张脸都变了。“别告诉别人我对着一幅肖像笑了。”
# en: Ask what he wants to be
opt.right.label [3ac212] = 问他想成为什么样的人
# en: He's never been asked. "Not that," he says, nodding at the portrait. Then, after a long time: "A teacher. Small school. Somewhere nobody's ever heard of my father." He walks off before you can answer. He looks lighter.
opt.right.say.1 [cdc4ed] = 从没人问过他。“不是那样。”他朝肖像点点头。过了很久：“老师。小学校。一个没人听说过我父亲的地方。”你还没来得及回答他就走开了。他看上去轻松了些。

@event bram_owns_up
# en: Bram Owns Up
title [84cd2d] = 布拉姆认了
# en: Bram finds you. "That exam," he says. "You saw. You never said." He's holding his sash. "I'm going to tell Thorne. I wanted you to know first. In case you wanted to stop me, I suppose." He doesn't look like he wants to be stopped.
text [262f3a] = 布拉姆找到你。“那场考试，”他说，“你看见了。你从没说出去。”他手里攥着他的绶带。“我要去告诉索恩。我想先让你知道。万一你想拦着我呢，我猜。”他看上去并不想被拦。
# en: A big student in a prefect's sash standing in front of a professor's desk, cap in hand, another student waiting outside the door.
scene [da84e6] = 一个佩着级长绶带的高大学生站在教授的书桌前，手里捏着帽子，另一个学生在门外等着。
# en: Go in with him
opt.left.label [1e8eec] = 陪他进去
# en: You stand by the door while he tells Thorne everything. Thorne listens, takes the sash, looks at it for a while, and hands it back. "Resit in a month," he says. "Wear it like you mean it." Bram walks out shaking. "Don't," he says. "Don't make it weird." You don't.
opt.left.say.1 [8a1d6e] = 你站在门边，他把一切告诉了索恩。索恩听完，拿过绶带看了一会儿，又递了回去。“一个月后补考，”他说，“戴着它，要名副其实。”布拉姆出来时在发抖。“别，”他说，“别弄得怪怪的。”你没有。
# en: Tell him it's past
opt.right.label [46f041] = 告诉他都过去了
# en: "It's done," you say. "Leave it." He hesitates, then puts the sash back on. You can see it sits differently. He doesn't cheat again; you'd bet on it. He doesn't forget, either.
opt.right.say.1 [0054bd] = “都过去了，”你说，“算了吧。”他犹豫了一下，把绶带重新戴上。你看得出它戴起来不一样了。他不会再作弊了，你敢打赌。他也不会忘。

@event bram_become_close
# en: Not Weird
title [e43d2f] = 不怪
# en: It's 3am and you can't sleep. Bram is on the stable fence, sash in his lap. "Night rounds," he says, which is a lie; rounds ended at midnight. "Sit if you want. Don't talk if you don't want." You sit. After a while he says, "You're the only one who didn't believe I was him."
text [2bab87] = 凌晨三点你睡不着。布拉姆坐在马厩的栅栏上，绶带搁在膝头。“夜间巡查。”他说——这是谎话，巡查午夜就结束了。“想坐就坐。不想说话就别说。”你坐下了。过了一会儿他说：“只有你不信我就是他。”
# en: A big student sitting on the stable fence at 3am beside another, a red sash folded in his lap, the hippogriffs asleep behind them.
scene [46193b] = 凌晨三点，一个高大的学生和另一个人并肩坐在马厩栅栏上，膝上叠着一条红色绶带，身后的鹰头马身有翼兽都睡着了。
# en: Leave him be
opt.left.label [ce4663] = 让他一个人待着
# en: You sit a while longer and then go. He says goodnight like it's an order. In the morning your demerits for the week have been crossed out, with no explanation.
opt.left.say.1 [ac99ab] = 你又坐了一会儿就走了。他道晚安道得像下命令。第二天早上，你这一周的记过全被划掉了，没有任何解释。
# en: Stay until morning
opt.right.label [d46a70] = 陪到天亮
# en: You stay. He talks about his mother, who's kind and doesn't say much, and the dog he had as a boy, and what he's afraid of, which is everything. At sunrise he says, "This is weird." Then: "It's fine. It's fine if it's weird."
opt.right.say.1 [ec831b] = 你留下了。他讲他母亲，和善、话不多；讲他小时候养的狗；讲他害怕什么——什么都怕。日出时他说：“这很怪。”然后：“没事。怪就怪吧。”

@event ilse_frozen_coins
# en: Coins That Freeze
title [28bf39] = 会结冰的硬币
# en: Ilse is at Mabel's counter again, glaring at a coin that has frozen to the wood. Mabel is pouring hot water on it. It isn't working. "It does this," Ilse says, through her teeth. "When I'm cross. I'm cross because it does this."
text [ca3584] = 伊尔泽又站在梅布尔的柜台前，瞪着一枚冻在木头上的硬币。梅布尔在往上浇热水。不管用。“它就是会这样，”伊尔泽咬着牙说，“我一生气就这样。而我生气就是因为它这样。”
# en: A teashop counter with a coin frozen to the wood, a girl in white furs glaring at it, a teashop owner holding a kettle over it hopefully.
scene [32ad34] = 茶馆柜台上冻着一枚硬币，一个穿白裘的女孩瞪着它，茶馆老板娘满怀希望地提着水壶往上浇。
# en: Pay, and warm the coin
opt.left.label [79b381] = 替她付，把硬币焐热
# en: You pay. Then you take the frozen coin and carry it in your pocket all afternoon, and give it back to her warm. She looks at it for a long time. "That's stupid," she says. She keeps it, separately from the others.
opt.left.say.1 [dc9f20] = 你付了钱。然后你拿走那枚冻住的硬币，揣在口袋里一整个下午，焐热了还给她。她盯着它看了很久。“真傻。”她说。她把它和别的硬币分开收着。
# en: Make her laugh until it thaws
opt.right.label [8dcdc7] = 逗她笑到它化开
# en: You do Thorne's voice. Then Bram's. On Bram, the coin cracks free of the counter with a pop, and Ilse makes a noise she clearly hadn't planned to make. "Again," she says. "No. Don't. Again."
opt.right.say.1 [a97a64] = 你学索恩说话。又学布拉姆。学到布拉姆时，硬币啪的一声从柜台上脱开了，伊尔泽发出一个显然不在她计划中的声音。“再来，”她说，“不。别。再来。”

@event ilse_private_storm
# en: Her Weather
title [ff0fd8] = 她的天气
# en: Ilse's private snowstorm follows her about the village. You've learned to read it. {~Today it's thick and sideways, which means stay away.|Today it's three flakes, slow, which means something's wrong and she won't say what.}
text [834dc1] = 伊尔泽的私人暴风雪跟着她在镇上走来走去。你已经学会读它了。{~今天它又密又斜，意思是离远点。|今天只有三片雪，慢慢地落，意思是出了什么事，她不肯说。}
# en: A girl in white furs walking through the village under a small private snowstorm that follows her, a second student stepping under it with her.
scene [8bc63e] = 一个穿白裘的女孩在镇上走着，头顶跟着一场小小的私人暴风雪，另一个学生走进雪里和她并肩。
# en: Step under it with her
opt.left.label [c53c7d] = 走进雪里陪她
# en: {~You walk beside her, inside the storm, getting snowed on. She doesn't say anything. After a street, the snow slows. After two, it stops. "Don't read it," she says. "It's rude." You read it anyway. It says: better.|You walk with her, getting snow down your collar. At the bridge she says, "My brother used to do that," and the three flakes become one, and then none.}
opt.left.say.1 [bb577e] = {~你走在她身边，在暴风雪里，被雪落了一身。她什么都没说。走过一条街，雪慢了。走过两条，雪停了。“别读它，”她说，“没礼貌。”你还是读了。它说的是：好些了。|你陪着她走，雪钻进你的领口。走到桥边她说：“我哥哥以前也这样。”三片雪变成一片，然后一片也没有了。}
# en: Wait it out at a distance
opt.right.label [31a6ec] = 远远地等它过去
# en: {~You give her room. The storm passes in an hour. She nods to you later across the square, which, for Ilse, is an apology for the weather.|You let her be. Later, a single snowflake lands on your sleeve, perfectly formed, and doesn't melt until you're indoors. You think it's a thank you.}
opt.right.say.1 [98b638] = {~你给她留出空间。一个钟头后暴风雪过去了。后来她隔着广场冲你点了点头——对伊尔泽来说，这是为天气道歉。|你由她去。后来一片雪花落在你袖子上，形状完美，直到你进了屋才化。你觉得这是一声谢谢。}

@event ilse_frost_craft_trade
# en: A Fair Trade
title [e62624] = 公平交换
# en: "Teach me something," Ilse says, at the pond. "Something of yours. I taught you frost. It's your turn. Something that isn't useful." She seems to think that's the hardest kind.
text [87b9f2] = “教我点东西，”伊尔泽在池塘边说，“你的东西。我教了你霜术。该你了。教点没用的。”她似乎觉得这是最难的一种。
# en: A frozen village pond, a girl in white furs teaching another student to throw a ring of frost across the ice, both breathing clouds.
scene [b40f88] = 结冰的镇上池塘边，一个穿白裘的女孩教另一个学生在冰面上甩出一圈霜，两人都呵着白气。
# en: Teach her a card game
opt.left.label [25b4a6] = 教她一种纸牌游戏
# en: You teach her a card game from home. She's terrible, and then, suddenly, ruthless. She beats you six times running on the ice and laughs out loud, once, before she catches herself. "That's not useful," she says. "Good."
opt.left.say.1 [d65397] = 你教她一种家乡的纸牌游戏。她先是糟透了，然后突然变得冷酷无情。她在冰上连赢你六局，还笑出了声，就一次，随即收住了。“这没用，”她说，“很好。”
# en: Teach her to skip stones
opt.right.label [ff3bdd] = 教她打水漂
# en: There's no open water, so you skip stones across the ice. Hers go further. Of course they do. She counts every bounce out loud, in Northern, and makes you count yours too.
opt.right.say.1 [b8980f] = 没有开冻的水面，你们就在冰上打水漂。她的漂得更远。当然了。她用北境话大声数着每一跳，还让你也数你的。

@event ilse_become_close
# en: Not a Trick
title [81c3ce] = 不是把戏
# en: It's 3am. You walk down to the shore, and Ilse is already there, on the ice, under her own small snowfall. "You keep being kind," she says, not looking at you. "I keep waiting to find out what it's for."
text [d867ed] = 凌晨三点。你走到湖岸边，伊尔泽已经在那里了，站在冰上，头顶下着她自己的小雪。“你一直对我好，”她没看你，“我一直在等着看这是为了什么。”
# en: A girl in white furs and a student sitting on the frozen lakeshore at 3am under a sky full of stars, snow falling very gently around only the two of them.
scene [d6d0be] = 凌晨三点结冰的湖岸，一个穿白裘的女孩和一个学生坐在满天星斗下，雪只在两人周围非常轻柔地飘落。
# en: Tell her it isn't for anything, and go
opt.left.label [f82cc3] = 告诉她不为什么，然后离开
# en: "Everything's for something," she says. But she lets you go without an argument, which is new. In the morning there's a small perfect snowflake on your windowsill that doesn't melt.
opt.left.say.1 [3dc34c] = “什么都是为了什么。”她说。可她没争辩就让你走了，这是头一回。第二天早上，你的窗台上有一片完美的小雪花，没有融化。
# en: Stay, and let her wait
opt.right.label [4eec40] = 留下来，让她等
# en: You stay. Neither of you says much. Around dawn the snow around her changes: it starts falling on you too, gently, the same as on her. She notices. "Oh," she says, very quietly, as if she's just learned a word. "Oh. It isn't a trick."
opt.right.say.1 [a766c9] = 你留下了。你们都没说什么。快天亮时，她周围的雪变了：雪也开始轻轻落在你身上，和落在她身上一样。她注意到了。“哦，”她非常轻地说，像刚学会一个词，“哦。不是把戏。”
